  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An integer array is called arithmetic if it is composed of **no fewer than three elements** and if the difference between any two consecutive elements is the same.\n\n* As an example, `[1,3,5,7,9]`, `[7,7,7,7]`, and `[3,-1,-5,-9]` are arithmetic sequences.\n\nWith an integer array `nums`, output *the number of arithmetic **subarrays** of* `nums`.\n\nA **subarray** is a contiguous subsequence of the array.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,4]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: We have 3 arithmetic slices in nums: [1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4] and [1,2,3,4] itself.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1]\nOutput: 0\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 5000`\n* `-1000 <= nums[i] <= 1000`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
